{
  "_readme": "Canonical examples of the routing and naming rule that skills/build-item/scripts/routing.py implements. scripts/tests/routing.sh runs every case through the helper. A repository with its own implementation of the rule should vendor this file and run every case through that implementation, so the two can never silently disagree. A target case's `config` is deep-merged over the top-level `config` (a null replaces); `expect` is the helper's output without its `reason`. A case with `error: true` must be refused as malformed (the helper exits 2), which is different from `kind: refuse`, a valid answer. A case marked `inputValidation: true` tests only the helper's JSON input checks; an implementation whose types already rule that input out may skip it.",
